================================================================================
 The nuclear charge model                                             t = 2.62 s
================================================================================
   default model                                              point
   this run's model                              gaussian (visscher-dyall-1997, main isotopes)
   point-nucleus SCF energy                       -128.512061726104  Eh
   finite-nucleus SCF energy                      -128.512027483796  Eh
   difference                                             3.424e-05  Eh   (positive: a spread-out nucleus attracts less)
   shift in the spin-free operator                        3.233e-07   (relative)
   shift in the spin-orbit operator                       3.858e-08   (relative)
   The effect is concentrated at the nucleus and grows steeply with Z: it is
   beyond any comparison at neon and reaches ~3e-3 of a mercury j-splitting.
   It is the first thing to match against a four-component program, several
   of which default to a Gaussian nucleus where Kuiva defaults to a point.
   The model is written into the Hamiltonian's provenance, so a property
   file made from this run says which nucleus it describes.

